  "reason": "The strongest evidence shows scvi_n200 as the dominant RNA encoder (0.725 vs ~0.52 for scgpt), with transformer+weighted as the best aggregation/fusion pair (0.7250 for config_027). The one major untested variable in this top region is the image encoder: all top results use imagenet_vit_l, but resnet50 has never been paired with scvi_n200. Config_015 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) directly tests whether the image encoder choice meaningfully affects performance when the RNA encoder and architecture are already optimal. If resnet50 matches imagenet_vit_l, it confirms we've found the plateau and the final experiment can focus on fine-tuning; if it lags significantly, it validates imagenet_vit_l as essential and rules out that direction. With only 2 experiments remaining, this is the highest-information experiment: it either confirms the current best is near-optimal or opens a new avenue, making it the best use of the next slot."
